      "id": "ERQ-LG-Q-9008",
      "q": "In two hypothetical steady states, the public holds no currency and banks have a fixed required-reserve ratio of 10 percent. The observed deposit-to-reserve ratio falls from 8 to 5. Assume all reserves are either required or deliberately held as excess reserves. Which diagnosis fits both observations?",
