      "id": 2005,
      "q": "Before an election, elected officials demand an immediate interest-rate cut while inflation remains above the central bank's target. The bank is free to choose its policy tools but must pursue publicly established goals and explain its decisions. How may the bank respond to the demand for a rate cut?",
      "options": [
        "The bank may reject the requested cut on inflation grounds while explaining how its decision serves its assigned goals",
        "The bank must grant the requested cut because public accountability transfers each rate decision to elected officials",
        "The bank may avoid the rate decision by unilaterally raising income-tax rates instead",
        "The bank may reject the requested cut without regard to its assigned goals or any duty to explain its decision"
      ],
