      "id": 9110,
      "q": "A central bank plans a $600 deposit contraction using an assumed deposit multiplier of 10. Later evidence puts the actual multiplier at 4, with no change in that estimate. Under the actual multiplier, how many reserves must it remove in total? Suppose the resulting disinflation lowers inflation from 6% to 4% and produces output losses of 2% and 1% of annual potential GDP in successive years. What sacrifice ratio follows, and would an equal reserve removal through a different tool alone guarantee a lower output cost?",
