      "q": "A negative demand shock creates a $1040 recessionary gap with falling inflation; capacity is unchanged. Assume the price level is fixed and MPC is 0.75. An increase in government purchases of $260 can take effect immediately, or the same program can take effect after the gap is forecast to close. Would the program close the recessionary gap if it took effect immediately, and what risk would it create if it took effect after recovery?",
      "options": [
        "The shock is adverse supply, so immediate purchases necessarily reduce inflation while restoring output",
        "The immediate program matches the current gap; the delayed one risks excess demand after recovery",
        "Both programs match every future gap because the multiplier makes timing irrelevant",
        "The immediate program is contractionary; the delayed program becomes expansionary solely because time passes"
      ],
