      "bossStage": "final",
      "q": "Use π = πe − (u − 5) + s, where π is actual inflation, πe is expected inflation, u is unemployment, and s is the number of percentage points a temporary supply shock adds to inflation. Rates are in percent. Actual inflation is 6% and unemployment is 5%. One analyst estimates πe = 6 and s = 0; another estimates πe = 4 and s = 2. Expected inflation remains at each analyst's estimated rate next year, while the temporary supply shock ends and unemployment stays at its natural rate. What additional information would help determine which inflation forecast is appropriate?",
