      "repairSkill": "long_run_adjustment",
      "commonError": "Incorrect inference: Use the original natural rate forever; reforms cannot affect a long-run unemployment benchmark.",
      "feedback": "If real labor-market structure changes, the natural benchmark can change. Persistence of lower unemployment then need not refute the expectations-adjusted Phillips model; the reform's effect must be separated from the temporary demand surprise.",
      "aHash": "d08fdd9b7657e07b016cd632137f6e1f75a535f52eba4b8ed293432cb33a9e46",
      "canonicalId": "PM2A-LRPC-LB-018",
      "primaryConceptId": "long-run-phillips-curve",
